{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/45513-vehicles-in-the-hedge","id":45513,"title":"Vehicles in The Hedge?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-09T05:20:40-08:00","id":45513,"title":"Vehicles in The Hedge?","content":"Are there any rules out there for vehicles in Changeling? Or should they be handled like creatures?<br /> <br /> Madcap chases on fae-built contraptions are on my mind. Clockwork spider-sedans, grasshopper like motorcycles, walking houses and airships are all on my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 01-09-2014, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T07:10:23-08:00","id":45564,"title":"","content":"I think you want the Fae Mount Merit (Rites of Spring p. 89).<br /> <br /> Walking houses are explicitly mentioned in the writeup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T10:20:11-08:00","id":45691,"title":"","content":"The basic vehicle rules are in the World of Darkness corebook, page 141.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T17:51:29-08:00","id":47158,"title":"","content":"There's also the Mobile Hollow merit in... either Swords at Dawn or Dancers in the Dusk, I forget which. That can be used if you wanted, say, a hedge airship the whole Motley lives on and crews. <br /> <br /> But yeah, generally it'll be a Fae Mount using the vehicle rules in the core. If you're trying to use mortal cars in the Hedge, they'll be unreliable - as I recall, the deeper you go in the Hedge, the less reliable technology gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T18:15:50-08:00","id":47170,"title":"","content":"&quot;Rumor has it, if you go deep enough in the Hedge with a car, it'll break down. This wouldn't be all that out of the ordinary save what happens later; it becomes an inviting home for hobs and hobgoblins of many sorts, which too is not out of the ordinary. Until the door or window or trunk slams down on a stray toe or finger. From there on out, they're damned. Damned to be a were-car; driving down hobgoblins and changelings alike, seeking to spread their lonley, abandoned curse to all. On nights of the mad moon if you listen closely enough, you can hear their forlorn, lonely car honks as they run over prey and leave wreckage of the lives of survivors. Don't try to camp out in abandoned vehicles in the Hedge, you'll regret it.&quot; ~ Twiddles Crumbcoat; Hedgewarden.<br /> <br /> Because, Futurama and the Hedge, and Christine and Bender-like killer cars roaming through it begs to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T10:31:35-08:00","id":49102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/45513-vehicles-in-the-hedge?p=47170#post47170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Rumor has it, if you go deep enough in the Hedge with a car, it'll break down. This wouldn't be all that out of the ordinary save what happens later; it becomes an inviting home for hobs and hobgoblins of many sorts, which too is not out of the ordinary. Until the door or window or trunk slams down on a stray toe or finger. From there on out, they're damned. Damned to be a were-car; driving down hobgoblins and changelings alike, seeking to spread their lonley, abandoned curse to all. On nights of the mad moon if you listen closely enough, you can hear their forlorn, lonely car honks as they run over prey and leave wreckage of the lives of survivors. Don't try to camp out in abandoned vehicles in the Hedge, you'll regret it.&quot; ~ Twiddles Crumbcoat; Hedgewarden.<br /> <br /> Because, Futurama and the Hedge, and Christine and Bender-like killer cars roaming through it begs to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems remarkably fitting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T09:27:27-08:00","id":57473,"title":"","content":"In my chronicle the players had to locate a starter for One-Hand Sam, preferably from a military vehicle. They travelled to Tampa and found out, that the local Summer Court keeps hedge side of MacDill is populated by agandonned military vehicles that have &quot;fallen through the gaps on the pavement&quot; and ended up in Hedge. Being machines built for war and then denied of their purpose they have become marauding hobgoblins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2095-daider-santo","name":"Daider Santo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}